  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1000.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1002.48 Open space/conservation subdivision",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1002.48 “Open space/conservation subdivision” means a purely residential subdivision of a tract of land, where:\n\n(a) A number of housing units are clustered on lots with dimensions and frontages reduced from minimum lot sizes required by Env-Wq 1005.03;\n\n(b) The dwelling unit density of the tract as a whole is equal to the density achieved by the lot sizing criteria of Env-Wq 1005.03 based on soil types and slopes; and\n\n(c) All land that is not housing lots is preserved as open space.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1 and #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1000) #11184, eff 10-1-16; ss by #14486, eff 2-1-26, EXPIRES: 2-1-36 (formerly Env-Wq 1002.45)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1000.html"
